    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφ-άδιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀναφάδιος</span> which does not occur, v.
			sq.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>public,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γάμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					6.288
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> acc. fem.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφαδίην</span> as Adv., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφαδόν</span>
			, <i>publicly, openly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.356
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				90
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
